From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:20:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 83/83] web-app: fit the phone recording row on one line, show
 the meter again
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 0074 phone layout wrapped the recorder onto two rows and both were
mostly empty: row 1 held pause/mic/timer then ~160px of gap before the
picker and the original-audio pill, row 2 held ~200px of gap before
Cancel/OK. The gap was the level meter, which the `max-width: 400px`
block hid while its container kept `flex: 1` — so a phone recording
showed no level feedback at all, and the space it would have used sat
empty one row below.

Two things forced the wrap, neither load-bearing:

  - `.originalAudioPill` is ~110px of a 390px row, and it toggles an
    encoding preference rather than driving the recording.
  - `.cancel` / `.stopRecording` are pinned to `width: 85px`, ~40px more
    than either label needs.

Dropping both leaves pause+mic+timer+meter+picker+cancel+ok at roughly
353px of a 380px content box, so the row fits on one line and the meter
no longer has to be hidden to make room. The `max-width: 400px` block
goes with it.

The pill is hidden on phones, not removed, so the toggle needs a second
home: the mic menu now carries it as a `menuitemcheckbox` row, and the
picker renders whenever the experimental recorder is on instead of only
when a second microphone is enumerated — otherwise a single-mic phone
would have no way to reach it.

Button height goes 32px -> 40px while the fixed width goes away. 32px is
under the 44px touch-target guidance, and a mis-tap on Cancel discards
the recording.
